{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"SUSE-SU-2026:4954-1","published":"2026-10-30T16:20:13Z","modified":"2026-11-02T17:23:10.113104458Z","related":["CVE-2026-107929","CVE-2026-11856","CVE-2026-18924","CVE-2026-19931","CVE-2026-80255","CVE-2026-82209","CVE-2026-86409","CVE-2026-86410","CVE-2026-86414","CVE-2026-87862","CVE-2026-87863","CVE-2026-87864","CVE-2026-8932","CVE-2026-92386","CVE-2026-92387","CVE-2026-92388","CVE-2026-92389","CVE-2026-92390","CVE-2026-92391","CVE-2026-92392","CVE-2026-94266"],"upstream":["CVE-2026-107929","CVE-2026-11856","CVE-2026-18924","CVE-2026-19931","CVE-2026-80255","CVE-2026-82209","CVE-2026-86409","CVE-2026-86410","CVE-2026-86414","CVE-2026-87862","CVE-2026-87863","CVE-2026-87864","CVE-2026-8932","CVE-2026-92386","CVE-2026-92387","CVE-2026-92388","CVE-2026-92389","CVE-2026-92390","CVE-2026-92391","CVE-2026-92392","CVE-2026-94266"],"summary":"Security update for curl","details":"This update for curl fixes the following issues:\n\n- CVE-2026-8932: incomplete mTLS config matching in conn reuse (bsc#1268414).\n- CVE-2026-11856: cross-origin Digest auth state leak (bsc#1268426).\n- CVE-2026-18924: HTTP/2 server push UAF (bsc#1277477).\n- CVE-2026-19931: Negotiate ambient user conn reuse (bsc#1277478).\n- CVE-2026-80255: secure cookie attribute bypass with tab (bsc#1277482).\n- CVE-2026-82209: domain-scoped PSL domain cookie (bsc#1278173).\n- CVE-2026-86409: stale SigV4 headers sent unintended (bsc#1285031).\n- CVE-2026-86410: redirect to SFTP or SCP bypasses host verification (bsc#1285030).\n- CVE-2026-86414: leaking host credentials to HTTP proxy (bsc#1285026).\n- CVE-2026-87862: HSTS cache import drops longer-lived child (bsc#1285023).\n- CVE-2026-87863: HSTS response erases persisted entries (bsc#1285022).\n- CVE-2026-87864: IMAP APPEND plus CRLF conversion command injection (bsc#1285021).\n- CVE-2026-92386: server-set cookie aborts cookie jar load (bsc#1285018).\n- CVE-2026-92387: never-ending loop via server response omission (bsc#1285017).\n- CVE-2026-92388: FTP wildcard write callback mixup (bsc#1285016).\n- CVE-2026-92389: TFTP direction confusion (bsc#1285015).\n- CVE-2026-92390: -J no-clobber guarantee bypassed with 103 early hints (bsc#1285014).\n- CVE-2026-92391: curl_mime_free stack overflow by recursion (bsc#1285013).\n- CVE-2026-92392: HTTP/2 upload Use-After-Free (bsc#1285012).\n- CVE-2026-94266: password leak in CURLINFO_EFFECTIVE_URL (bsc#1285010).\n- CVE-2026-107929: local interface connection reuse mixup (bsc#1285008).\n","affected":[{"package":{"name":"curl","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux Enterprise Installer Updates 15 SP4","purl":"pkg:rpm/suse/curl&distro=SUSE%20Linux%20Enterprise%20Installer%20Updates%2015%20SP4"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"8.14.1-150400.5.98.1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"binaries":[{"libcurl4":"8.14.1-150400.5.98.1"}]},"database_specific":{"source":"https://ftp.suse.com/pub/projects/security/osv/SUSE-SU-2026:4954-1.json"}},{"package":{"name":"curl","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux Enterprise Installer Updates 15 SP5","purl":"pkg:rpm/suse/curl&distro=SUSE%20Linux%20Enterprise%20Installer%20Updates%2015%20SP5"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"8.14.1-150400.5.98.1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"binaries":[{"libcurl4":"8.14.1-150400.5.98.1"}]},"database_specific":{"source":"https://ftp.suse.com/pub/projects/security/osv/SUSE-SU-2026:4954-1.json"}},{"package":{"name":"curl","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux Enterprise Micro 5.3","purl":"pkg:rpm/suse/curl&distro=SUSE%20Linux%20Enterprise%20Micro%205.3"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"8.14.1-150400.5.98.1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"binaries":[{"curl":"8.14.1-150400.5.98.1","libcurl4":"8.14.1-150400.5.98.1"}]},"database_specific":{"source":"https://ftp.suse.com/pub/projects/security/osv/SUSE-SU-2026:4954-1.json"}},{"package":{"name":"curl","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux Enterprise Micro 5.4","purl":"pkg:rpm/suse/curl&distro=SUSE%20Linux%20E